cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use OpenBridge or its white paper in research or policy work, please cite it as below.
  OpenBridge is a prototype: its eligibility rules are drafts that experts have not verified.
type: software
title: 'OpenBridge: a privacy-first, open-source public benefits screener'
abstract: >-
  OpenBridge is an open-source web app that screens a household for several U.S. benefit programs
  at once (SNAP, Medicaid and CHIP, WIC, with LIHEAP and TANF in progress), explains every result
  in plain language with the calculation and its sources, and runs entirely on the user's device.
authors:
  - name: 'StarlingTek, LLC'
    email: openbridge@starlingtek.com
repository-code: 'https://github.com/UbiquitousKiwi/OpenBridge'
url: 'https://github.com/UbiquitousKiwi/OpenBridge/wiki'
license: AGPL-3.0-only
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-07-15'
keywords:
  - public benefits
  - civic technology
  - eligibility screening
  - SNAP
  - Medicaid
  - WIC
  - privacy
  - accessibility
